cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, cite the version archived by Zenodo and the relevant research documents."
title: "Cyclic Fueter Theory: Lean 4 Formalization of Selected Results"
version: "0.6.0"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kurokawa-rijio/Cyclic-Fueter-Theory-Lean"
authors:
  - family-names: Kurokawa
    given-names: Ryojiro
abstract: >-
  This software repository contains Lean 4 source files developed in connection with
  the Cyclic Fueter Theory (CFT) research program. It formalizes selected algebraic
  and geometric statements involving quaternionic algebra, Fueter-type operators,
  matrix and spinor constructions, quantum-geometric identities, Cartan-frame
  calculations, the reduced Einstein–Yang–Mills action and its four-dimensional
  field equations, distributional junction conditions, characteristic evolution and
  constraint-propagation identities, zero-mode calculations, and
  selected Wess–Zumino–Witten (WZW)-related formulas, and consequences of the action
  principle for the Einstein–Yang–Mills dumbbell, including its junction, conformal
  frame and smoothness, the shape of the dumbbell, a reduced action with canonical
  constraints and a Wheeler–DeWitt equation for the spherically symmetric sector,
  and a two-dimensional Dirac field. The repository includes an
  author-maintained status ledger of 182 items in α-I–α-XV, each recorded as
  kinematics, action, and dynamics. Status labels
  describe the current formalization scope and are not independent certification or
  peer review of the corresponding research claims. Lean verifies theorem conclusions
  from declared assumptions and imported results; formalization does not by itself
  validate the physical interpretation or applicability of external results.
